To say the least this is a poor strategy.  I usualy play a Samurai,
but lately I have been playing a wizard.  The Saumurai has THE best
fighting stats and has a killer kick, but the wizard comes with
lots of neat magical junk and he can usualy be built up pretty
quick.  Now what you do is get a pick-axe (you can nearly always
find one around level 3, all you have to do is find a dwarf and
kill him for it [very easy to do]) then find a shop and cut a door
four spaces from the corner farthest from the main door, then cut
another one opposet so it looks like this:
     / 
----+------
|../....@.+
|./.......|
|?........|
+.........|
|.........|
-----------

Now just get everything directly to the side of one of the doors
like the scroll above and stand in the door way and proceed to kick
all the items into the other doorway like the / indicates.  This
way you quickly steal everything from the store and you dont get
the shop keeper mad at you.  You can walk back in and sell the
stuff back to him and steal it again...  Or you can set everything
in a pile and use a wand of teleport on it and just go and find the
merchandise which will be placed randomley around the level.
Neither of these tactics will get you in trouble with the cops or
the shop keeper.  MUCH safer.




